### Design Rationale Summary

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| find spruce_planks | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task → player must see the target. Target at center of spruce pillar (-5, 1, 2). |
| find oak_pressure_plate | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task → player must see the target. Target at pressure plate location (3, 0, 5). |
| craft to dark_oak_trapdoor | inventory_has | Craft task → crafted item ends up in inventory. Player starts with 0 trapdoors, needs ≥1. |
| find green_concrete | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task → player must see the target. Target at center of concrete columns (6, 1, 10). |

**Key decisions:**
- All "find" tasks use `position_near_with_facing` (preferred for find/locate/observe tasks per guidelines)
- `max_distance=16` is generous — all targets are within 10 blocks of spawn, so the player will naturally be within range when exploring
- `facing_tolerance=60` ensures the player is actually looking toward the target (not just nearby with back turned)
- The craft task uses `inventory_has` with bare item name `"dark_oak_trapdoor"` (no minecraft: prefix per guidelines)
- All spatial coordinates use `coordinate_frame="spawn_relative"` as required

